DataSerializer's PassportRow:
```
interface PassportRow {
  id: string;
  user_id: string;
  gender?: string;
  expiry_date?: string;
  issue_date?: string;
  issue_place?: string;
  photo_uri?: string;
  is_primary?: number;
  created_at?: string;
  updated_at?: string;
  [key: string]: unknown;
}
```

Differences: local has `string | null` for the optional fields vs just `string` in DataSerializer. And local has `number | null` for `is_primary` vs just `number` in DataSerializer. These differences make them incompatible.

And for PassportCountryRow:
Local:
```
type PassportCountryRow = {
  passport_id: string;
  country_code: string;
  visa_required?: number;
  max_stay_days?: number | null;
  notes?: string | null;
  created_at?: string;
  [key: string]: unknown;
};
```

DataSerializer's:
```
interface PassportCountryRow {
